# The build context, shared by BOTH images — and that "both" is the thing that
# went wrong once already.
#
# This file was written for deploy/web/Dockerfile alone, which copies output/web
# and the Caddyfile and nothing else, so it denied everything and allowed those
# two back. Then deploy/api/Dockerfile arrived, and its very first instruction —
# COPY server/package.json — failed with
#
#     "/server/package.json": not found
#
# because Docker had already stripped server/ out of the context. The Dockerfile
# was correct, the path existed in the repo, and the build still could not see
# it. That failure names the file it wanted and says nothing about why, and
# nothing catches it until a Railway build is already running.
#
# So: every top-level directory any Dockerfile COPYs from has to be allowed back
# in here, and server/test/dockerignore.test.ts asserts exactly that by reading
# the COPY lines out of both Dockerfiles.
*

# deploy/web/Dockerfile: the Caddyfile and the prebuilt Godot export.
!deploy/
!output/
output/linux/
output/*.zip

# deploy/api/Dockerfile: the API sources it compiles. Not node_modules — the
# image runs its own `npm ci` — and not dist, which is built inside the image.
!server/
server/node_modules/
server/dist/
